nd that's you know that's the goal  i mean you you don't have an option  there because if  for instance you find you know two  million dollars worth of  waste a hundred to one on that is twenty  thousand dollars  and and when you try to solve a problem  for twenty thousand dollars to get rid  of two million dollars of waste  it uh  you know it may be it it's hard  so i'm not saying this is this is easy  but it forces people to think of  the problem in terms of uh  getting a high return on the on the  problem so for instance if you  are working on a project and you only  get 20 to one  do you think that the management of the  company is going to be mad at you  no they're not that's a good deal  because what is 20 to one it says you're  going to pay off the project in two and  a half weeks  pretty good deal so  my reason for from the beginning for  doing it is because i tried a couple of  numbers and they kept getting bigger and  bigger  and so initially i was doing  uh 20 to one and then i realized man we  can get 50 to one  pretty easily and it moved it up to 50  to wood  and then when i got to the bigger  companies i cranked it up to 101  and then the solution is  the uh  you know when when you're that's the  fourth step and the  fifth step is your presentation to the  ceo  and that presentation consists of  making sure that you've covered  what it is you're going to do what kind  of implementation plan you've got  all the details of how you're going to  get rid of that problem or make it  a substantial part of it go away and  then  the last step is the actual  implementation and metrics  that measure the success of the project  over the year  and that that's uh and that's it and  but you know it's not this you know one  of the things that  people say you know they say hey lynn  i've got a friend of mine who's the  operations manager and he  would like to do something and uh if  it's a small company i would say  let's get to meet the ceo because  uh problem solving